It's been a while since I last updated, right? I’m posting here to inform you that the final stage of the game's development has [b]returned to normal[/b]. I had to take a [b]sudden break[/b] from development due to several issues, but they have been resolved. The next update will bring [b]NUMEROUS bug fixes[/b] that unfortunately piled up all this time without a fix update, in addition to the short, yet dynamic, story mode where I try to cover as much as the game can offer up to this point. [b]I don’t have a set date[/b] for the release of this update, but I’ll give you a brief summary of what it will include:

- Missions for the game’s story;
- Final Boss;
- Various bug fixes;

Maybe not along with this update, but I still owe more cards to expand the range of possible builds in the game. Most likely, I’ll release them with the final update of the game, which will be version [b]1.0[/b].

A [b]DEMO[/b] is also being considered along with the end of early access, so those who have doubts about whether the game will appeal to them or not can test it for themselves.

In this patch I only made small changes to the layout of the pause menu and end of game screen. The rest of what is being implemented is still being tested so that it can be posted with as few bugs as possible. Changes below:

- Pause menu pages and end-game screen now functional with shortcuts (keyboard or controller) to improve page-related functionality;

- I made a slight change to the position of the restart and exit buttons on the end of game screen;



Here's a quick [b]peek[/b] at the next mini boss planned for the next update:

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/44843544/447b7ad52563c919f11dcad13320260cc178631f.png[/img]

[b]Many[/b] fixes in this update. Pages to view all collected cards have finally been added in the pause and death screens. More information on the changes below:

- Fixed the size of the upgrade stats in the shop, which were larger than the defined size, resulting in them being cut off;

- The Top Hat had an error in the upgrade information;

- There was a bug related to the pause menu that caused the mouse to lock up;

- Enemies now spawn in greater numbers and in less time, but with attack intervals revised to match this change;

- Bug in Meowtech that made it immortal while using its power;

- Meowtech was holding the staves off-center with one of the accessories;

- Added pages in the pause menu and post-death screen to view all the cards collected during gameplay;

- Damage from slugs and the boss has been revised;

- Crystal projectiles from the first staff no longer pass through enemies. This feature was made for one of the accessories;

- Adjusted the positioning of certain elements in the pause menu;

- Some new cards had display issues in the pause menu when the player restarted the game without returning to the lobby;

- The death screen was also affected by the mouse bug;

- Attempt to fix the issue of the boss stairs going past the designated area;

- Projectiles now only bounce off walls with a specific staff, to emphasize different gameplay styles and balance the game;

- Sound of enemy explosions/deaths when restarting/returning to the lobby has been fixed;

- Upgrading items with the mouse did not trigger the achievement for the first upgrade;

- Orbs had the wrong damage (same problem as the daggers, which has also been fixed);

- Orbs had outdated code. Now they prioritize the boss in damage situations and switch to common enemies when the boss cannot be damaged;

- Problem with maximum attack speed values if the player exceeded the set limit. When combined with Chopper's power, it reduced the total attack speed instead of reverting to the original value before the buff;

[b]The shop now has more information[/b], and certain issues related to the last update have been resolved. More details below:

- Quality of life improvements, such as brief descriptions of characters, weapons, and accessories in the shop;

- The accessory upgrade area now displays their respective effects and what those effects will be after upgrading;

- Reduced the number of silver tokens dropped, as it was causing performance issues in later waves;

- Silver tokens are now transparent so they don't obstruct enemy projectiles and hinder visibility;

- Fixed a bug with "Absorb" where, if the boss's damage exceeded the absorb value, it would result in a negative value;

- Corrected some cards with incorrect values;

- Projectile acceleration was not resetting after the match ended;

- Fixed a typo in the game over screen;

- Some accessory effects had coding errors that have been fixed;

- The increasing cost of rerolls as waves progressed was not functioning. It is now working as intended;

- The exit game menu from the lobby was not working with the "SPACE" button;

For various reasons, I will have to postpone the content I had planned for today to next week. [b]HOWEVER[/b], it will be for a good cause. I am working on making the coin drop system fairer so that this mechanic, which will be essential for building a build, can be used more frequently. Below are the details of what will be added in the next update 0.2.0:

- The possibility to [b]reroll[/b] cards and upgrade their rarity with tokens collected during the match. I am looking to encourage the use of this mechanic by improving the gold and silver token drop system. This requires more testing and, after release, collecting feedback;

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/44843544/e031aa0f3e76f3d9f4a6d0518da8473dceef2121.png[/img]

- Accessories will have unique effects, each with its own focus and benefit for the player, making accessories more essential than just increasing the overall strength of the character;

- I found a bug in the dagger code that caused them to always deal 1 damage instead of the correct damage including the sum of card upgrades;

This week, I didn't add much, but several existing aspects of the game were tweaked, which I believe will contribute to a more rewarding gameplay experience for players. Details are provided below.

- The accuracy attribute was displayed incorrectly for players in the in-game pause menu, giving the impression that the accuracy value increased very little with each upgrade. However, this was just a visual issue and has been fixed;

- Added YELLOW/ORANGE color to represent the maximum value of an attribute in the pause menu, giving players a better sense of which attributes are already maximized;

- Arrows indicating ground enemies (slugs) now have an alert icon next to them to emphasize the danger and an audio effect for easier identification;

- Some cards had outdated descriptions, which could cause players to avoid picking certain cards purely due to the low value, discouraging them from testing new cards;

- Increased the base value of tokens (gold) obtained when eliminating mini bosses. The value increases progressively;

- Staff abilities (right button) now apply the effect in the same way as Theodore's normal projectiles while his ability is active;

- Added a new mechanic to the racket staff and an impact feedback sound effect;

- There was a priority conflict for the bee staff about what to attack in boss fights. This has been corrected in the code;

- Significantly increased the maximum capacity of bees (with cards);

- Adjusted enemy damage scaling values again;

- Fixed a visual bug that did not display the base projectile damage of staves on the mini boss;

- Damage values now stay on the screen longer for easier visualization;

- Fixed a bug that did not display the damage dealt with the base projectile of staves on the mini boss;

For the focus next week, I intend to complete the effects system for accessories, which will allow for many more strategic/ gameplay approaches.

In this update, I made small changes that will have a significant impact on gameplay, such as unlocking the rarity system regardless of the wave you are on and reducing the base attack frequency of enemies, which increases as waves progress. The rest of the changes are listed below.

- By request, I changed the color of the outline lines in the tutorial that indicate where the player needs to go in the shop to make it easier to see what needs to be purchased;

- Revised the card rarity system, making the RNG factor much more apparent. Previously, the rolls followed maximum limits on the card level according to the wave. I changed it so that it is possible to get any card level up to level 4 even in wave 1, but you will need to be lucky for that to happen;

- Enemy damage was scaling very abruptly and nonsensically, so I [b]COMPLETELY[/b] revised the system to have fixed values for health and damage increases that alternate every 10 waves (each mini boss);

- Increased base values of the cards, as well as their subsequent upgrades, to make higher-level cards more meaningful with more significant values;

- Damage from the boss "Coffin" and ground enemies (slugs) now only deals damage if the "absorb" effect is not active. Previously, the damage would bypass the "absorb" card effect;

I thank everyone who provided me with feedback and suggestions. I emphasize again that any questions, criticism, or suggestions can be sent in the discussions tab here on Steam or in the official game server found on the store page.

[b]Note: I am alternating game updates to once a week, preferably on Fridays. This way, I can focus calmly on each aspect I am working on and reduce the frequency of quick updates that introduce new bugs due to lack of testing.[/b]

- It is now possible to advance Riggs' dialogue by holding the interaction button;

- Fixed the issue where the basic projectile damage of the staves was not showing;

- Readjusted base values and texts of the "Dagger" card;

- Ground enemies (slugs) would teleport to the player's location if the player left the game paused for a certain time;

Regarding game development, I am currently working on the mechanics of the next mini boss.

[b]Note: I am aware of a case where the game crashes abruptly as soon as it starts. I am looking for ways to identify the cause, and any information shared in this case will be extremely helpful for future correction.[/b]

- Enemy and boss health scaling redone, as they were too exorbitant and I didn't notice due to lack of testing;

- Initial visual bug related to the laser for the controller;

- Card rarity system changed again to test feedback;

- Reformulated the way staff accuracy is presented, ranging from 0 to 100. Higher values mean less projectile evasion;

[b]NOTICE[/b]

As I have reformulated the accuracy system and along with it adjusted the base values of the staves, I [u][b]STRONGLY RECOMMEND[/b][/u] creating a new save to avoid any bugs related to old saves. Along with this notice, I would like to make it clear that the save created is automatically linked to the version when it was created. To check your save version, just pause the game in the lobby with ESC or P and check the version number in the lower left corner. When there are major changes such as adding items and more features to the game, it may be necessary to create a new save to fully enjoy the new content, but when that time comes, I will always give a notice, as I am doing now. I also recommend not deleting the old saves but rather creating new ones and seeing if the changes made are worth restarting the game from scratch.

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/44843544/91e74ae6c128587a4318397d3e31193e262f3236.png[/img]

Small changes, with the main focus on readjusting shop/upgrade values to match the increased coin drops in matches. The rest of the changes are listed below.

- Prices for cats/staves/accessories and their respective upgrades increased to match previous updates that made earning coins easier;

- Health scaling fixed (values were too high and not properly adjusted);

- Readjusted chance for higher rarity cards to appear in any wave;

- Laser added when the player is using a controller to make aiming easier;

- Option to toggle the player's view to "with arcade," which is the default used so far and comes standard, and the option "without arcade," which will remove these details from the screen;

- Selection border on the current card;

- Visual health bar size of the mini boss fixed (was going off the screen);

- Some minor changes to the rarity system;

- Visual bug of the lobby button layouts overlapping in some scenarios;

Resolved performance issues, enemy damage/health scaling, a revision of the "Absorb" card, among others. Below, I will detail what was actually changed in this patch.

- Resolved performance issues related to the effect of the "Explotion" card, which caused extensive resource usage, resulting in poor performance for players;

- The "Explotion" card will now dissipate on the first impact, whether it hits an enemy or walls. This way, the game is cleaner from projectiles instead of the previously common bullet rain;

- Fixed a coding error related to enemy damage scaling and slightly increased their respective values to better align the difficulty with the previous change of reducing the number of enemies and spawn time;

- Increased the font size of the card descriptions for easier reading;

- The "Absorb" card was very overpowered due to the amount of shield granted per stack, and it also allowed for indefinite stacking, making the game easier than intended. A limit has been set so that only one card can be taken at a time. In the next card pools, while the player has a shield from "Absorb," new versions will not appear as long as there are uses left in the current one;

- Increased the mini boss's health significantly on lower floors;

Several bugs related to card selection and a new enemy quantity/spawn time approach being implemented for testing.

- Total number of enemies needed to go through a wave reduced from wave 10 onwards, trying to make the game more dynamic;

- Issues related to card selection with staffs other than Crystal Staff fixed;

- Tutorial added as an "?" on  the right side of the PLAY button.(yes, finally);

- Silver Tokens drop revised;

- Was possible to trigger mutiple achievements with a bug related to upgrades;

I am happy to finally be releasing our first game in its early access version. The scope began 2 years ago with a lot of inspiration from Seraph Last Stand and Vampire Survivors, and we managed to create our own identity over time. I am immensely grateful, now and always, to my friends for giving constructive feedback for the game's slow but steady evolution. As the patch, I added and fixed certain bugs related to the interface and quality of life, such as a more visible crosshair and enemy projectiles, as well as the addition of a new currency, the SILVER TOKEN, which will serve as more visual feedback for the player that their progress is not in vain, even if they are having difficulty getting through the first waves. I thank you again for your support and sincerely hope that the game reaches a final state as close as possible to my original vision and that players approve and critique my future choices.

[b]PATCH 0.1.5 Change List[/b]

- Updated crosshair with clearer contrast for easier localization;
- Button layout near the respective interaction areas;
- Added SILVER TOKEN: every 100 coins collected is converted into 1 GOLDEN TOKEN;
- Increased coin drops from enemies (more silver tokens);
- Visual/audio feedback for coin collection;
- Revised enemy projectiles for better visibility during the match;
- Fixed bug in Catfield related to its power bar filling;
- Reduced speed of the green projectile (fast);
- Red Arrow indicates the direction where ground enemies spawn;
- Increased invincibility duration after Snowflake's dash;

[b]FIXED BUGS[/b]

- If the game remained paused for a certain time, the position of the enemies would bug, possibly leaving them out of the player's field of vision, indefinitely stalling the wave;

- Fixed bugs related to the total number of deaths required to advance to new waves;

- Game crash when returning to the lobby from within a run by pressing ENTER instead of using the mouse;

- Catfield filling the special bar TOO MUCH with particles (e.g., poison);

[b]KNOW BUGS[/b]

Transition ladder to the boss area moving infinitely, never stopping properly in the correct position;
